package Libraries.Fabrication

use Libraries.Language.Errors.InvalidArgumentError
use Libraries.Language.Errors.FileNotFoundError
use Libraries.System.TextFile

/*
The ArgumentChecker class validates the values handed to the fabrication
libraries' Set actions, so a bad setting stops the program right where it
was given instead of as a hang or a strange print much later (a line width of
0, for example, makes every fill loop run forever).

A failed check stops with an InvalidArgumentError (or a FileNotFoundError)
whose message says which action, which value and what was wrong, so callers
can also catch it with check / detect.

Attribute: Example

    use Libraries.Fabrication.ArgumentChecker
    use Libraries.Language.Errors.InvalidArgumentError

    class Main
        action Main
            ArgumentChecker checker
            check
                checker:RequirePositive("Example:SetWidth width", 0)
            detect e is InvalidArgumentError
                output e:GetErrorMessage()
                // Example:SetWidth width must be greater than 0, but was 0.0
            end
        end
    end
*/
class ArgumentChecker
    /*
    Stops unless the value is greater than 0.

    Attribute: Parameter name What is being checked, such as "PathGenerator:SetLineWidth width".
    Attribute: Parameter value The value to check.
    */
    action RequirePositive(text name, number value)
        if not (value > 0)
            Fail(name + " must be greater than 0, but was " + value)
        end
    end

    /*
    Stops unless the value is at least the minimum.

    Attribute: Parameter name What is being checked.
    Attribute: Parameter value The value to check.
    Attribute: Parameter minimum The smallest allowed value.
    */
    action RequireAtLeast(text name, number value, number minimum)
        if not (value >= minimum)
            Fail(name + " must be at least " + minimum + ", but was " + value)
        end
    end

    /*
    Stops unless minimum <= value <= maximum.

    Attribute: Parameter name What is being checked.
    Attribute: Parameter value The value to check.
    Attribute: Parameter minimum The smallest allowed value.
    Attribute: Parameter maximum The largest allowed value.
    */
    action RequireRange(text name, number value, number minimum, number maximum)
        if not (value >= minimum and value <= maximum)
            Fail(name + " must be between " + minimum + " and " + maximum + ", but was " + value)
        end
    end

    /*
    Stops with a FileNotFoundError unless the path names an existing file.
    The message gives the absolute path, since relative paths start in the
    folder the program runs in, which is easy to get wrong.

    Attribute: Parameter name What the file is for, such as "start G-code".
    Attribute: Parameter path The path to check.
    */
    action RequireFile(text name, text path)
        TextFile files
        if path = "" or not files:Exists(path)
            FileNotFoundError error
            error:SetPath(path)
            error:SetErrorMessage(name + " file not found: '" + path + "' (looked for " + files:GetAbsolutePath(path) + ")")
            alert(error)
        end
    end

    /*
    Stops with an InvalidArgumentError carrying this message.

    Attribute: Parameter message What was wrong.
    */
    action Fail(text message)
        InvalidArgumentError error
        error:SetErrorMessage(message)
        alert(error)
    end
end
